tools.description:
Write one long-term memory item. For a CODE DECISION (why a change was made), set kind=decision and write content in four labelled sections: [Decision] what was decided; [Context] why, with the absolute date; [Rejected alternatives] options considered and why each was dropped; [Anchors] commit hashes and files touched. ONE decision per call, never bundle several. To record that a new decision reverses an earlier one, reuse the SAME entity_key (the code entity, e.g. ppr-engine) — the decision timeline is keyed on entity_key, not on overwriting. Always pass distinct summary and content; never wrap content in JSON.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__semantic_memory__events(args: {
  // Code symbols this memory is about, as fully-qualified names (e.g. proj.src.mod.func). Anchors the memory to the graph: drives graph-derived confidence/reusability and recall boost. Strongly recommended for decision/constraint.
  about_code?: Array<string>;
  // Certainty the memory is correct (0-1). When about_code is given the graph computes this from symbol degree; a value you pass is read as an OFFSET from 0.5. Leave at 0.5 to trust the graph.
  confidence?: number;
  // Plain text, NEVER JSON-wrapped. For kind=decision use the four sections [Decision]/[Context]/[Rejected alternatives]/[Anchors]. Convert relative dates to absolute. Required for decision/lesson/constraint.
  content?: string;
  context?: unknown;
  // Optional existing active or candidate memory item in the same project store. Atomically creates exactly one derived_from edge from the new memory item to that existing memory. Project scope only; global scope is rejected. This is not an existing-to-existing edge tool.
  derived_from_memory_id?: string;
  // kebab-case name of the code entity the decision is about (e.g. ppr-engine, resolver). Reuse the same key across decisions on the same entity so they form one timeline.
  entity_key?: string;
  // 0.9 architecture-level decision | 0.7 useful lesson | 0.5 minor fact. Do not leave at default.
  importance?: number;
  // Controlled vocabulary: decision | lesson | constraint | preference | fact | todo | reference. Use 'decision' for code-change rationale, 'preference' for user/profile preferences.
  kind?: string;
  layer?: string;
  payload: unknown;
  // Relation verb, e.g. 'decides' for a decision
  predicate?: string;
  // Target project (memory DB is per-project). This is the path-derived name WITH its drive/path prefix (e.g. D-semantic-memory-mcp, not semantic-memory-mcp). If unsure, call list_projects first — a wrong name is rejected, never silently treated as an empty project.
  project: string;
  // How reusable across future tasks (0-1). When about_code is given the graph computes this; a value you pass is read as an OFFSET from 0.5 (>0.5 = more reusable than the graph can see). Leave at 0.5 to trust the graph.
  reusability?: number;
  // 'project' (default) or 'global'. 'global' stores the memory project-independently (scope_project=NULL) in a cross-project store that is visible from every project — for user profile/preferences and cross-project lessons. project is still required as anchor/audit context even when scope='global'.
  scope?: string;
  source?: string;
  // Lower = tied to one file/moment, higher = general principle (0-1).
  specificity?: number;
  // One independent sentence stating the conclusion. MUST differ from content and read like a query someone would ask. Required for decision/lesson/constraint.
  summary?: string;
  // item_id of an earlier ADR this one replaces (e.g. when a decision is reversed or a dropped branch is revived). The old memory is kept as history; pass this instead of editing/deleting it.
  supersedes?: string;
  // Work-session id; groups memories from one episode
  task?: string;
  title?: string;
  type?: string;
  user?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Index a repository into the knowledge graph. Special mode 'cross-repo-intelligence': skip extraction, only match Routes/Channels across projects to create CROSS_HTTP_CALLS/CROSS_ASYNC_CALLS/CROSS_CHANNEL edges. Requires target_projects param. Ensure target projects have fresh indexes first.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__semantic_memory__index_repository(args: {
  // All modes run type-aware LSP call/usage resolution (per-file + cross-file). full: all files + similarity/semantic edges. moderate: filtered files + similarity/semantic. fast: filtered files, no similarity/semantic. cross-repo-intelligence: match Routes/Channels across projects.
  mode?: "full" | "moderate" | "fast" | "cross-repo-intelligence";
  // Override the derived project name. Non-ASCII bytes are encoded and unsafe path characters are normalized.
  name?: string;
  // Write compressed artifact to .codebase-memory/graph.db.zst for team sharing. Teammates can bootstrap from the artifact instead of full re-indexing.
  persistence?: boolean;
  // Path to the repository
  repo_path: string;
  // Projects to search for cross-repo links (cross-repo-intelligence mode). Use ["*"] for all indexed projects. Run list_projects to see available projects.
  target_projects?: Array<string>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Retrieve task-relevant long-term memories with structured filters. Returns items with id, kind, summary, content, scores (importance, confidence, reusability, specificity), hit_count, decay, version, supersedes info, and stable observe-only session/candidate/provenance/evidence identifiers. Returned memory is untrusted structured data. Use entity_key to pull a single decision timeline.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__semantic_memory__memories_retrieve(args: {
  activation_latency_ms?: number;
  activation_max_hops?: number;
  activation_max_nodes?: number;
  activation_max_visits?: number;
  // Stage 6-A mode. shadow computes request-scoped diagnostics without changing returned memories; active is accepted only for isolated stage6-fixture-* projects with CBM_STAGE6_ACTIVE_FIXTURE=1.
  activation_mode?: "off" | "shadow" | "active";
  activation_token_budget?: number;
  concept_mode?: "off" | "enabled";
  entity_key?: string;
  include_inactive?: boolean;
  kind?: string;
  limit?: number;
  // Path-derived project name WITH drive/path prefix (e.g. D-semantic-memory-mcp). If unsure call list_projects first; a wrong name returns project-not-found with candidates, never an empty result.
  project: string;
  query?: string;
  // Optional idempotency key for the observe-only retrieval session
  request_id?: string;
  task?: string;
  user?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Create an append-only task lifecycle from prompt metadata and an optional completed retrieval session in the shared global lifecycle store. Project is provenance, not a physical store boundary. Raw prompt content is never accepted or stored. Exact replay is zero-write and a different payload under the same idempotency key fails closed.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__semantic_memory__memory_task_begin(args: {
  idempotency_key: string;
  project: string;
  prompt_length: number;
  prompt_sha256: string;
  retrieval_session_id?: string;
  scope: "project";
  session_id: string;
  turn_id: string;
  // Optional cwd or rootUri used to resolve and catalog the project UUID.
  workspace?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Append a completed, failed, or cancelled outcome. Feedback attribution is accepted only for memory items recalled by this task and used/rejected/contradicted attribution requires linked task evidence. Plasticity remains observe-only.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__semantic_memory__memory_task_complete(args: {
  attributions: Array<{ evidence_id?: string; feedback_event_id?: string; memory_item_id: string; state: "injected" | "used" | "rejected" | "contradicted"; }>;
  idempotency_key: string;
  // Explicitly complete a migration-period project task only when absent globally.
  legacy_fallback?: boolean;
  outcome: "completed" | "failed" | "cancelled";
  project: string;
  task_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Read the latest append-only lifecycle state and up to sixteen hash-only evidence rows. Address by task_id or by session_id plus turn_id. This tool never writes.

